# Shell scripts must always check out with LF line endings, even on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true. A CRLF shebang line (`#!/bin/sh\r`) breaks POSIX shell execution inside
# Linux containers — discovered via infra/postgres-init/01-create-databases.sh, which is bind-
# mounted into the Postgres container by infra/docker-compose.yml and silently failed to run
# ("/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter") on a Windows checkout before this file existed.
*.sh text eol=lf
